.TH ES 1M "Root Computers Ltd."
.SH NAME
es \- print ROOTexec statistics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B es
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I es\^
is a utility provided with the
.I ROOTexec package to print statistics on
how well the package is working. It is only available under versions
1.2 and onwards.
.I es\^
prints one line of output containing:
count \- the number of reads called,
(one for a normal program, two for a pure executable program),
saved \- the number of transfers saved,
holes \- the number of one block "holes" found in the program,
max \- the number of attempts to exceed MAXCOUNT in param.h,
size \- the number of attempts to exceed execsize in conf.c,
cache \- the number of blocks read from the Unix standard cache,
contig \- the number of contigous portions read
wait \- the number of waits for execbuf to be freed.
.PP
Each number is based since system startup time.
.SH FILES
/unix
/dev/mem
.SH SEE ALSO
fscr(1m).
